From 2d4c7b69305f31a1209c8c18fa625858ed45e760 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hibreak <hibreak@localhost>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 02:53:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] sf: black-and-white enhancement pass for e-ink panels

The HiBreak Pro's panel shows black and white only in its normal and fast
modes; the kernel dithers everything in between. Grey or coloured text,
thin grey icons, hairlines and every anti-aliased edge therefore come out
as dither noise, in every app.

With debug.sf.eink_enhance (strength in percent), the render engine runs one
more pass over the composed frame of the built-in display: each pixel is
compared with the mean of its surroundings (12 taps on two rings), and the
further it is from that mean, the more it is pushed to pure black or white.
Text and lines of any colour on any background become solid, edges become
hard, and flat or smooth areas (fills, photos) are left to the dither.
Only while the composer's refresh mode is a black-and-white one; the grey
modes keep their anti-aliasing. Screenshots and virtual displays are not
touched (debug.sf.eink_enhance.capture=1 includes it, for tuning).

The same pass applies the text contrast (vendor.xrz.hibreak_contrast_black /
_white, set by HiBreakParts), after the enhancement, so that light
hairlines are still seen before the stretch turns them white.

Change-Id: I853f6b44f3c34023f3440a8705e4c23b2805c372
---
